    "title": "Tesla's Optimus Can't Build Its Own Hands Yet - NewsBreak",
    "text": "9 hours ago Tesla turned over the Fremont factory’s old Model S and Model X lines to Optimus this year. It now turns out several hundred of the humanoid robots a week. That’s about ten times the pace from second-quarter testing. Managers want a continuous line that can do more than 1,000 a week by the end of 2026. The longer-term number is 20,000. Read full article",
